1
00:00:00,084 --> 00:00:02,084
(Mike:)You remember
the Thanksgiving game

2
00:00:02,253 --> 00:00:04,093
(Mike:)when it snowed in Dallas?

3
00:00:04,255 --> 00:00:07,725
Nineteen-ninety three. Leon Lett blew
the game in the final seconds

4
00:00:07,892 --> 00:00:09,702
(Sheldon:)and the Dolphins
emerged victorious.

5
00:00:09,861 --> 00:00:12,701
(Sheldon:)Then I finally got to do
my calculus.

6
00:00:12,864 --> 00:00:16,174
(Mike:)I was so pissed,
I wanted to shoot my TV.

7
00:00:16,334 --> 00:00:18,114
(Sheldon:)So was my dad.

8
00:00:18,269 --> 00:00:19,369
And than he did.

9
00:00:21,439 --> 00:00:23,249
(Howard:)-Anyone need a beer?
-Yeah.

10
00:00:23,408 --> 00:00:24,858
(Howard:)Thank God.

11
00:00:25,777 --> 00:00:28,587
(Mike:)So, does your dad
still live in Texas?

12
00:00:28,746 --> 00:00:31,356
(Leonard:)No.
He died when I was 14.

13
00:00:32,550 --> 00:00:34,390
(Mike:)I'm sorry to hear that.

14
00:00:34,552 --> 00:00:36,792
(Sheldon:)So was the man who owned
the local liquor store.

15
00:00:38,556 --> 00:00:40,466
(Sheldon:)He cried and cried.

16
00:00:41,726 --> 00:00:44,566
(Howard:)-Here you go.
-Thanks.

17
00:00:45,463 --> 00:00:48,133
(Mike:)So, if your dad died
when you were 14,

18
00:00:48,299 --> 00:00:51,079
(Mike:)you were never old enough
to have a beer with the man.

19
00:00:51,469 --> 00:00:52,469
(Sheldon:)No, sir.

20
00:00:52,737 --> 00:00:55,547
(Sheldon:)He did try to give me one
for my high school graduation,

21
00:00:55,707 --> 00:01:03,027
(Sheldon:)but I was 11 and my mom said, no.

